60721,"title":"","content":"It's been written for ages, but there are always some bottlenecks in the process.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:32:35-07:00","id":889261,"title":"","content":"So it's out to backers. How is it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:29:55-07:00","id":889290,"title":"","content":"The first story alone is absolutely fantastic. Riveting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:42:43-07:00","id":889291,"title":"","content":"The second story was pretty great too. I feel like these writers really <i>get</i> what makes Mummy awesome. (Of course Malcolm does, that goes without saying.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:13:18-07:00","id":892129,"title":"","content":"Wow, I'm surprised this thread hasn't been more active! I have so far only read the first story, but WOW what a doozy!! It took me a while to see how the story ties everything together, but once it came together, it was so impactful. I loved seeing the story from the perspective of Shuanksen and Deceived. Some bits of description really were flavorful, like the Deceived being caught shapeshifting, and how the Deceived's Temakh and personality blur. And that alchemist has had that coming since the Core book--serves her right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:59:28-07:00","id":892156,"title":"","content":"This is one time of many that I wish I had known about and backed Mummy when I had the chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T03:45:18-07:00","id":892413,"title":"","content":"Well, to increase the suspense until the book is made public, it isn't &quot;just&quot; a fiction collection. It introduces a new plot point that can be dropped into any Mummy chronicle--the Blue Nile, a mythical Relic claimed by many Guilds to be their own. Supposedly, all Arisen would recognize it, and all felt its creation, even if they can't remember what it is and what it does. Also, the fiction seems to have some interesting ideas in it. It clarifies what a sekhem Sorcerer is capable of, and their place in Arisen society. It nicely explores mesoamerican Mummies. It addresses how many different lifestyles and personalities even low level mummies can have. But all the stories tie all of this around the basic, fundamental urge for mummies to seek Relics. Though, so far, no two of these stories has been about the &quot;same&quot; Blue Nile, they are in a way all about that Kepher-induced feeling of need, and about how a Relic's draw (especially a legendary relic) can shape stories in different ways.<br /> <br /> I do have a question that either a developer or a writer could answer for me. I noticed that in Father of Ab, the Nomarchs of LA are mortals. On the one hand, this feels like it could be a mistake on the writer's part. On the other hand, it seems like it'd make a lot of sense for various Deathless, with their brief descents, relying on long-lived humans to give their guild continuity. I couldve sworn all Nomarchs were Arisen, but seeing humans-as-nomarch brought a lot of interesting ideas to the table. (PS, sorry if this hasnt separated into two paragraphs. My mobile and this website have an odd relationship with regards to paragraphs and autocorrect)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T15:27:33-07:00","id":892823,"title":"","content":"I finished the anthology. It was really good, and I recommend it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: t